Package: igos-openssl-fips-provider
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, libssl3 (>= 3.0)
Description: OpenSSL FIPS 140-3 validated provider (CMVP #4985)
 Ships the pinned, pre-built OpenSSL 3.1.2 FIPS provider (fips.so) that holds
 NIST CMVP certificate #4985, installed into the OpenSSL provider module
 directory (ossl-modules/).
 .
 The provider is version-decoupled from the base library: this validated 3.1.2
 module loads against the system's OpenSSL 3.5 libcrypto. It is inert until
 activated — igOS switches OpenSSL to this provider on
 "set system option fips" (which runs "openssl fipsinstall" to self-test the
 module and generate /run/ssl/fipsmodule.cnf, then points openssl.cnf at it).
 .
 This package only installs the frozen, validated binary; it does not build or
 alter it. See docs/igos-fips-140-3-design.md (§7.5, §8.1).
